From 1e0290270be40a3e8bc93996d1842ede7a9f06ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tommy <tommy@pham.cc>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 05:09:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 46/55] GL backend: redundant state filter, batch key without
 unused registers, vertex ring

Three cuts of the GL thread's per-batch cost (~1000-1300 batches per fight frame):
- gs_gl_state_cache: the Api copy the renderer uses drops GL calls that would not
  change state (enables, blend, depth, viewport/scissor, program, uniforms per
  program, texture bindings per unit, texture parameters per texture, VAO/VBO,
  pixel store). Deletions forget what they held. PS2X_GL_STATE_CACHE=0: off.
- batchKey: primitives that differ only in registers the batch draw does not use
  (XYOFFSET is applied per vertex; fog colour, PRIM type/FGE/AA1/FIX/CTXT, PABE,
  SCANMSK, DIMX, DTHE, FBA, TEXCLUT, MIPTBP; texture registers of untextured
  primitives) join one batch. PS2X_GL_BATCH_KEY=0: whole-state match as before.
- vertices go to a persistently mapped 64 MB ring (four fenced quarters) instead
  of a glBufferData per batch. PS2X_GL_VERTEX_RING=0: glBufferData as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
